+  of a procedure, by its label and by its name, for a second branch whose ends both move when the first one is
+  rewritten, and for a branch in reach that a rewrite puts out of reach. The data is never executed; .lcomm is
+  written in place on Linux and elsewhere on some other targets. ttbz2.inc holds 36000 bytes of .ascii. }
 program ttbz2;
 
-{ 2 when bit 3 of x is clear, else 1; the tbz jumps forward across 36000 bytes of data }
+{ 2 when bit 3 of x is clear, else 1; the tbz jumps forward across 36000 bytes of .ascii }
